  "method_review": [
    "Exactly 32 predeclared windows (12 per primary and 4 per guard), with all retained in original order. Six adjacent same-seed pairs per primary, three AB and three BA, and alternating primary profile order.",
    "All 32 summary rows are accepted and valid; no behavior errors, generator limit or exclusions are reported. Collector independently asserts equal pair config hashes, actual executable hashes, complete cache proofs, and zero upstream requests during hits.",
    "Status helper reads progress/acceptance only. The frozen driver refuses an existing run.json and preserves incomplete/invalid runs. The collector computes secondary descriptive medians after completion; it does not alter primary CPU values.",
    "The reused estimator is byte-identical to the frozen SHA; the actual types controller is paired_tcp_records_phase.py, not the earlier paired_tcp_records.py.",
    "All six final/main ratios exceed one in both primary profiles. The higher candidate windows are retained, including 100-record pair 1 ratio 1.377756. Order-group medians differ notably for 1000 records (AB 1.218940, BA 1.067147); direction stays positive in both groups."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This local review independently recomputes from per-window retained integer cgroup deltas and completion counts in types-summary.json. cpu-points.json, latency binaries, and full original window files are only indexed at Oracle paths; this review did not re-read or re-hash those remote originals.",
    "The t intervals are per scenario and rely on independence/stability and an approximately appropriate paired-log model with only n=6. Alternation is balanced but deterministic, not randomized; VM neighbor/time effects are not excluded. The exact sign-flip p=0.03125 is descriptive, not a randomized-experiment proof.",
    "Both numerical lower bounds exceed 1 but neither exceeds 1.10. This supports increased CPU for these fixed Oracle workloads; it does not establish that the increase is at least 10%, nor equivalence, nor an allowed regression tolerance.",
    "The two-pair TCP/0 and UDP/1000 guards are descriptive; they cannot precisely attribute the residual increase or close ordinary TCP performance concerns. Do not subtract across different profiles to infer causality.",
    "All cached questions here are A and unrelated raw records are type 65401. They do not measure same-type name misses, ANY, many distinct raw types, arbitrary TCP workloads, saturated throughput, connection capacity, long-duration leakage, or physical router performance.",
    "The measured main and final artifacts differ by cumulative branch code and declared static-PIE build flags. These numbers cannot attribute cost to the type-summary change or any single commit/function.",
    "The retained 480 recursive cgroup observations are zero-throttle checks, not 480 independent statistical replicates. Only six window pairs enter each primary confidence interval."
  ]
